# Each line is a path prefix from the repository root, not a gitignore pattern: the
# packager drops a file whose path starts with a line (Play1Plugin's startsWith), so a
# glob matches nothing and a bare name such as `.gitignore` matches only at the root.
# Exclude project management artifacts from distribution
_bmad/
_bmad-output/
# docs/architecture/ holds internal design docs, docs/agents/ the topic guides
# AGENTS.md links, and docs/README.md the documentation catalog — all excluded.
# docs/user-guide/ is intentionally NOT excluded: it ships in the bundle so the
# in-app user-guide lookup can read it at runtime (Play.applicationPath/docs/user-guide/).
# Every other docs/ subdirectory is gitignored, and this task's file list comes
# from `git ls-files`, so only a file directly under docs/ needs its own line here.
docs/architecture/
docs/agents/
docs/README.md
test/
# The frozen ArchUnit capability allowlists (JCLAW-1152) are a build-time
# baseline read by test/CapabilityRulesTest, never by a running install.
archunit_store/
loadtest/
# The eval dataset (JCLAW-875) is a development measuring stick — the runner
# reads it from a checkout, never from a running install.
evals/
app/
frontend/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
Dockerfile
docker-entrypoint.sh
Jenkinsfile
Jenkinsfile.renovate
.distignore
.dockerignore
.gitignore
.gitattributes
sidecar/asr/.gitignore
sidecar/diarize/.gitignore
sidecar/fetch/.gitignore
sidecar/image/.gitignore
sidecar/stealth/.gitignore
sidecar/tts/.gitignore
sidecar/video/.gitignore
# Developer-only tooling — git hooks, dev container config, AI assistant
# state, the Renovate bot's dependency-update config, GitHub's repository
# settings and the jenv/asdf Java pin all belong to the source repo, not
# to a `play dist` tarball an end user unzips.
# Note: .play-version is NOT excluded — build.gradle.kts reads it at
# Gradle configure time (every `playStart` / `playRun` evaluation), so
# it must ship in the dist alongside build.gradle.kts itself.
.githooks/
.devcontainer/
.claude/
.sandcastle/
renovate.json5
.github/
.java-version
# Read only in test mode (%test.application.log.path) and by the release
# build's ProGuard step, neither of which runs in an install.
conf/log4j2-test.xml
conf/proguard-debug-strip.pro
# Build-time coverage artifacts (Jenkins only; not for the prod zip).
# bin/ + conf/jacoco-agent.properties ship in the source repo so the
# `%test.javaagent.path` line in conf/application.conf still resolves
# when someone runs `play autotest` from a fresh clone, but the
# generated jacoco.exec / jacoco.xml should never ride into prod.
jacoco.exec
jacoco.xml
bin/
conf/jacoco-agent.properties
# The config knob that regenerates archunit_store/'s frozen-violation
# baselines: read only by test/, which is already excluded, so it does not
# belong in a prod zip.
conf/archunit.properties
